#!python
# marketmaker.pyj - Minescript 5, Minecraft 26.3 (Fabric)
#
# \marketmaker   opens the menu (add items, switch them on/off, Scan spreads, Start). Run it again to stop.
#
# How it works:
#   1. Spread check: reads the best /orders buy price and the auction price of each item (3 reads, middle value)
#      and only buys when the profit is above your min profit %.
#   2. Buy: makes a buy order a little above the best one; re-bids if it gets outbid and it's still worth it.
#   3. Sell: collects the items and lists them on /ah at the cheapest other seller's price - never under them,
#      never under what the items cost you. Dumps are waited out; sales are seen right away from chat.
#   4. Round done: shows the profit, waits 15 s (\yes = next round now, \no = stop), then checks the spreads
#      again and picks the best item.
# Your items and menu settings are saved in marketmaker_list.csv.

